  OFFICIAL PRIME ROWS (e=1  =>  n | p-1  =>  p = 1 mod 2^41):
  ord_n(p) = 1  =>  every <p>-coset of (Z/n)^* is a SINGLETON
  =>  w_cov = 1 + (n-1) = n = 2^41.
  The window also obeys w <= r'+w = 2^40, so w < 2^40 < 2^41 ALWAYS.

  LEVEL-a THRESHOLDS AT e=1 PRIME ROWS (delta=1 at every level):
  the integrality gate p > 2^a passes for EVERY a <= 40 at live
  rows (log2 p >= 129.585); the threshold w_min(a) = 2^41-2^a+1
  is MINIMISED at the deepest level a = 40:
  best admissible level: a = 40, w_min = 1099511627777 = 2^40.00000
  every crossing instance has r' = 2^40 - w >= 1, i.e.
  w <= 2^40 - 1 = 1099511627775;  min_a w_min(a) - max w = 2.

